---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO_URL, url } from '../lib/records';
---
<Base title="About">
  <h1>About CCME</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The CCME (Connected Community Marine Estate) is a Muizenberg network of around 230 residents. Our shared purpose is to build a more connected community in Marine Estate.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are guided by Sociocracy, using consent-based decision-making so that everyone can take part and share ownership. We also use Nonviolent Communication (NVC) to build empathy and constructive dialogue. We draw on design thinking, asset-based community development, Open Space Technology and appreciative inquiry.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Connectors Circle is where newcomers begin and where community-wide decisions are made. Around it, special-interest circles let residents contribute where their interests and skills are strongest.
  </p>
  <h2>About this website</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    This site is the CCME's public record. It is made of plain files kept in a Git repository, so every
    change is saved with who made it and when.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Circles</strong>: the teams in the group, what each one is for, and who is in it.</li>
    <li><strong>Roles</strong>: who holds each role, and when the term ends. Past holders stay on the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Meetings</strong>: minutes of published meetings.</li>
    <li><strong>Decisions</strong>: what was proposed, what was agreed, and when it will be reviewed.</li>
    <li><strong>Actions</strong>: what someone has agreed to do, by when, and whether it is done.</li>
    <li><strong>People</strong>: who takes part, and what they hold.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the site is kept up to date</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each change is a commit in the Git repository, so the full history is kept.</li>
    <li>The site is rebuilt automatically whenever a change is saved, and every day.</li>
    <li>Daily checks flag overdue actions and role terms that end within 30 days, by opening a GitHub issue.</li>
    <li>Items marked members-only, and draft meetings, are left out of the public site entirely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to edit it</h2>
  <p>
    Editors use the admin page at <a href={url('admin/')}>the admin page</a>, which provides forms for each
    kind of record. The step-by-step guide is in
    <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/EDITING.md`}>EDITING.md</a> in the repository.
  </p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    The code and the content are open source under the MIT licence. Anyone can read the history, suggest a
    change or help maintain the site: <a href={REPO_URL}>{REPO_URL.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
